@startuml
title Chain of Responsibility / Chain / Pipeline

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Pass requests along a chain; let multiple objects try handling it.

**Motivation**:
Validation steps, authorization, event handling where multiple handlers may act or stop.

**Applicability**:
Multiple potential handlers; flexible routing; avoid hard-coded sender/receiver.

**Participants**:
Handler holds next; each decides to handle or pass on.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Loose coupling; reorder handlers; add/remove easily.
Cons: Hard to ensure an ultimate handler; debugging path.

**Implementation Notes**:
Return values to indicate handled vs pass-through; consider short-circuiting.

**Known Uses**:
Logging frameworks; GUI event handling; middleware pipelines.

**Related Patterns**:
Interceptor, Decorator, Command.

endlegend

abstract class Handler {
  -next : Handler
  +setNext(h: Handler) : Handler
  +handle(req: Request)
}

class ConcreteHandlerA
class ConcreteHandlerB

class Request

Handler <|-- ConcreteHandlerA
Handler <|-- ConcreteHandlerB
Handler o-- Handler : next
ConcreteHandlerA ..> Request
ConcreteHandlerB ..> Request
@enduml